REASON
The case relates to the proposed amendments in G)ntrol of NarcoticsSubstance (CNS) Act 1997. It is sbted that Control of Narcotics Sutrstance (CNS), Act,1997, completely covers the offences relating to Narcotics D-ugs, PsychotropicSubstances and Controlled Subsbnces, The illegal possessioo/ manufacturing, sale,purchase, distribution etc. of Narcotics Drug, Psychotropic Substances and (:ontrolledsubsbnces in an offence under Section 6 of CNS Act, 1997 and punishable under Section9 of CNS Act, 1997. The financinq of the trafflcking of Narcotlcs Drugs, PsychotropicSubstances and Controlled SubsEnces is an offence under Section 8 of CNS ,\ct, 1997and punishable under Section 9 of CNS Act, 1997. The Peshawar Hiq Court directed thefueral Govemment to make shict legislation to curb the use and sale of"methamphetamine", popularly known as "ice" and "crystal meth", since this cangerousdrug is destroying our young generation. It is also mentioned that the proposedamendments in CNS Act, 1997 cover adequate and reasonable punishment For illlcittrafficking of "methamphetamlne", a psychotropic subjstace. Moreo\€r, the punishmentfor all other lllicit drugs has also been reviewed, keeping in view the substance and{uantity of drugs. In addition to this, the punlshment for sale of arugs in educaBonalsetting has also been enhanced.
(Sardar Ali Muhammad Khan Mahar)Federdl Ministerfor Narcotics Control
